From: LinBox <linbox@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] LinBox box64: Android RELR tags in elfparser.c (v0.3.2..v0.4.1 layout)

Legacy-layout twin of 0002. The v0.3.x..v0.4.1 elfparser.c nests the
dynamic-tag switch one level DEEPER (16-space case indent inside the
extra { } block wrapping the DT_* loop), while 0002 carries the v0.4.2+
12-space form. Authored and dry-run verified against v0.3.8 exactly.

Applied with --fuzz=0 (box64 build.sh custom_patch since v3.3.34): with the
default fuzz=2, 0002's hunk can fuzzy-misplace the DT_ANDROID_RELR case under
case DT_VERDEFNUM on v0.3.8 (sandbox-verified corruption) - the strict gate
makes 0002/0003 self-select by exact layout match, one of the two always
applies (and 0004 covers elfparser32.c on every tag since v0.3.2).

Without the alias, NDK lld's DT_ANDROID_RELR (0x6fffe000/0x6fffe001/
0x6fffe003) packed relocations are silently skipped -> bionic wine
x86_64-unix/ntdll.so keeps raw .data self-pointers -> wineboot SIGSEGV
(see 0002's full writeup).
---
diff --git a/src/elfs/elfparser.c b/src/elfs/elfparser.c
--- a/src/elfs/elfparser.c
+++ b/src/elfs/elfparser.c
@@ -225,3 +225,4 @@
                 case DT_RELR:
+                case 0x6fffe000:  // DT_ANDROID_RELR (LinBox: bionic RELR tags, same encoding)
                     h->relr = ptr;
                     break;
@@ -228,3 +229,4 @@
                 case DT_RELRSZ:
+                case 0x6fffe001:  // DT_ANDROID_RELRSZ
                     h->relrsz = val;
                     break;
@@ -231,3 +232,4 @@
                 case DT_RELRENT:
+                case 0x6fffe003:  // DT_ANDROID_RELRENT
                     h->relrent = val;
                     break;
